Z||000000||mrfixit58||01-11-2001||03:56 PM||||I just wanted to pass along a thumbs-up to Rodney's Ball Joint Separater tool. It sepearates the ball joints from the spindle without damaging the ball joints or their dust boots. I don't know if he still offeres it but if he does, it works great.<P>I bought it a couple of years ago and when I did, I asked him if it would work on my 68 Camaro. He said it would but he would have to make me a longer separator bolt because the Camaro's ball joints were farther apart then the Fiero. HE DID THIS FOR ME AND DIDN'T EVEN CHARGE ME EXTRA! Can you say, "Customer Service!".<P>Well, this weekend I finally got around to working on the Camaro and his tool worked GREAT!<P>Just wanted to give credit where credit was due... thanks Rodney,<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000001||FieroJoe||01-11-2001||08:15 PM||||Yes, I too would definatly have to say that hes got a good thing going there.  A great buisness, and provider of hard to find replacement parts or just some cool stuff to add to your Fiero.  I've ordered from him twice so far, and have had no complaints at all!  Each order came very quickly!<P>Thanks Rodney!<BR><P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
